<title>A graphical approach to finding equilibria of discrete dynamical systems</title>

<p><ref>Video 1</ref> | <ref>Video 2</ref> | <ref>Transcripts</ref> </p>
<description>
By plotting the updating function and the diagonal, one can read off the equilibria from their intersections of the two graphs.
</description>


<section name="vid_section"><title>Video 2</title>
<p>The second video gives you another chance to see both the graphical and analytic approach to finding equilibria with another sample function.</p>

<figure suppressFigureNameInCaption="true">
<video youtube="S79I3vEbObk" size="large" aspectRatio="16/9" name="v2" />
<caption>Graphical approach to find equilibria of discrete dynamical systems</caption>
</figure>

<setup>
  <number name="timestamp1">198</number>
  <number name="timestamp2">208</number>
</setup>
  

<sideBySide margins="5%">
<div><p>Video credit achieved: <number displayDecimals="1">$v2RoundUp*100</number>%</p></div>

<div>
<p><updateValue type="number" target="$v2.time" newValue="$timestamp1" name="skipTo1">
  <label>Go to Key Moment 1</label>
</updateValue></p>
<updateValue type="text" triggerWith="$skipTo1" target="$v2.state" newValue="playing" name="playStamp1" />
</div>

<div>
<p><updateValue type="number" target="$v2.time" newValue="$timestamp2" name="skipTo2">
  <label>Go to Key Moment 2</label>
</updateValue>
<!--   <updateValue type="number" target="$v1.time" triggerWith="buttonLink2" newValue="$timestamp2" name="skipTo2b"/> -->
</p>

<updateValue type="text" triggerWith="$skipTo2" target="$v2.state" newValue="playing" name="playStamp2" />
<!-- <updateValue type="text" triggerWith="skipTo2b" target="v1" prop="state" newValue="playing"/> -->
</div>
</sideBySide>


<number name="v2RoundUp" hide="true">
  <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="$v2.fractionWatched > 0.9">1</case>
    <else>$v2.fractionWatched</else>
  </conditionalContent>
</number>

<answer hide="true" name="v2Credit">
  <award credit="$v2RoundUp"><when>true</when></award>
</answer>

<callAction triggerWith="$v2" target="$v2Credit" actionName="submitAnswer" />
  
<problem><title>Video 1 review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<setup>
  <boolean name="hidePoints">true</boolean>
  <boolean name="hideExercise2">true</boolean>
  <point hide="true" name="E1" fixed="true">(-2,-2)
    <label><m>(-2,-2)</m></label>
  </point>
  <point hide="true" name="E2" fixed="true">(1,1)
    <label><m>(1,1)</m></label>
  </point>
  <point hide="true" name="E3" fixed="true">(2,2)
    <label><m>(2,2)</m></label>
  </point>
</setup>
<p>How many equibilibria does the system shown in the graph below have?
  <answer name="vid2Review1">3</answer></p>
  

  <hint hide="$vid2Review1.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $vid2Review1.creditAchieved = 1 or $vid2Review1.numSubmissions >= 5">You can find a hint to this at <ref to="$vid_section">Key Moment 1</ref> in the video.</hint>

<hint hide="$vid2Review1.numSubmissions &lt; 5 or $vid2Review1.creditAchieved = 1">Look for all the locations on the graph where the graph of <m>f(x_n)</m> intersects the graph of <m>y = x</m>. How many places does this happen?
</hint>
  

<updateValue target="$hidePoints" newValue="false" type="boolean" triggerWhen="$vid2Review1.creditAchieved = 1" />

<updateValue target="$hideExercise2" newValue="false" type="boolean" triggerWhen="$vid2Review1 = 3" />
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true" hide="$hideExercise2"><title />
<p>Drag the equilibrium points labeled <m>E_1</m>, <m>E_2</m>, <m>E_3</m> to the correct locations on the graph. Click the button below when you are finished placing all points to check your work.</p>

  <answer submitLabel="Check Equilibrium Points" name="vid2Review2">
    <award unorderedCompare="true">
      <when><mathList>$E1 $E2 $E3</mathList> = <mathList>$p1 $p2 $p3</mathList>
      </when>
    </award>
  </answer>

   <hint hide="$vid2Review2.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $vid2Review2.creditAchieved = 1 or $vid2Review2.numSubmissions >= 5">You can find a hint to this at <ref to="$vid_section">Key Moment 2</ref> in the video.</hint>

<hint hide="$vid2Review2.numSubmissions &lt; 5 or $vid2Review2.creditAchieved = 1">See if you can slide each $p1.styleDescriptionWithNoun to each location where the two functions intersect. If you get close to an intersection point, the $p1.styleDescriptionWithNoun will snap into place.
</hint>
  </exercise>

  
<graph xmin="-4" ymin="-4" name="cubicGraph">
    <xLabel><m>x_n</m></xLabel>
    <yLabel><m>x_{n+1}</m></yLabel>
    <function applyStyleToLabel="true" name="f" fixed="true">
      x^3 - x^2 - 3x + 4
      <label><m>f(x_n)</m></label>
    </function>
    <line styleNumber="2" applyStyleToLabel="true" name="g" fixed="true">y = x
      <label><m>y = x</m></label>
    </line>
    <point hide="$hidePoints" name="p1" styleNumber="2">(6,6)
      <label><m>E_1</m></label>
      
        <attractTo threshold="0.1">$E1 $E2 $E3</attractTo>
        <constrainTo>$g</constrainTo>
      
    </point>
    <point hide="$hidePoints" name="p2" styleNumber="2">(7,7)
      <label><m>E_2</m></label>
      
        <attractTo threshold="0.1">$E1 $E2 $E3</attractTo>
        <constrainTo>$g</constrainTo>
      </point>
    <point hide="$hidePoints" name="p3" styleNumber="2">(8,8)
      <label><m>E_3</m></label>
      
        <attractTo threshold="0.1">$E1 $E2 $E3</attractTo>
        <constrainTo>$g</constrainTo>
      
    </point>
  </graph>


  
<solution>
  <graph xmin="-4" ymin="-4" name="solutionGraph">
    <xLabel><m>x_n</m></xLabel>
    <yLabel><m>x_{n+1}</m></yLabel>
    $f $g
    <point hide="false" styleNumber="2" extend="$E1" /> <point hide="false" styleNumber="2" extend="$E2" /> <point hide="false" styleNumber="2" extend="$E3" />
  </graph>
</solution>
  
</problem>
  
</section>
